 "かのうせい": "اِحْتِمَال (The quality of being possible.) / إِمْكَانِيَّة (A thing possible; that which may take place or come into being.) / إِمْكَانِيَّة (An option or choice, usually used in context with future events.)  [possibility]\nおそれ is often preferred for negative outcomes\nمثال: 彼女が電車に乗り遅れた可能性はあるでしょうか。\n→ Might she have missed her train? / وَعْد, وَعْدَة (An oath or affirmation; a vow.) / وَعَدَ, تَعَهَّدَ (To commit to (some action or outcome), or to assure (a person) of such commitmen) / بَشَّرَ (To give grounds for expectation, especially of something good.)  [promise] / اِحْتِمَال (The quality of being possible.) / إِمْكَانِيَّة (A thing possible; that which may take place or come into being.) / إِمْكَانِيَّة (An option or choice, usually used in context with future events.)  [possibility (modal property of a proposition containing no logical contradiction)]",
