 "から": "مِن (Used to indicate source or provenance.) / مِن, عَنْ (Indicating differentiation.)  [from]\nindicates starting location or time, or point of separation; as ...～...まで when setting a scope\nمثال: 彼は九時から五時半まで働く。\n→ He works from nine to five-thirty. / عَبْر (From one side or end of (something) to the other.) / خِلَالَ, عَبْرَ (From one side or end of (something) to the other.) / فِي (Amidst or surrounded by (while moving).) / بِوَاسِطَة (By means of.)  [through (e.g. a window, door)]\nindicates passage or transit\nمثال: 彼は窓から入ってきた。\n→ He came in through the window. / لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]\nafter a verb or i-adjective; だ～ after a noun or na-adjective\nمثال: 彼の部屋に明かりがついているから、彼は帰宅したにちがいない。\n→ Since the light in his room is on, he must have come home. / مِن (Used to indicate source or provenance.) / مِن, عَنْ (Indicating differentiation.)  [from (as in \"made from\")]\nindicates constituency\nمثال: 水は酸素と水素からできている。\n→ Water consists of hydrogen and oxygen.",
